THE FOUR NEW NUMBERS, AND WHY THESE FOUR
----------------------------------------
Every one is a documented failure mode of this harness, not a statistic someone
might like.

  model 12 · 8m12s   Where the time WENT. The reported collapse was 51 model
  tools 14 · 1s      calls and 22.5 minutes against tool calls costing under a
                     second. Two numbers side by side say "this is not a tool
                     problem" instantly; neither alone says anything.

  failed 4           How much of the work did not land. Four failed patches in
                     a turn is the elision-poisoning signature from 2026-08-22,
                     and it was previously only visible by reading every line.

  repeated           `contract_status x8` is the signature of a stuck run. Live
    contract_status x8   2026-08-21 a 3B did exactly that, and the only way to
                     notice was to count rows. Amber from three, because a tool
                     called three times in one turn is thrashing, not working.

Model duration now rides on the event as `model_seconds` rather than being
parsed back out of "model responded in 41s" - a display should not be reading
English to get a number.


COLOUR THAT IS LOAD-BEARING
---------------------------
Green / amber / red mean one thing everywhere: fine, getting tight, out of
room. Same 60/80 thresholds `CliTurnRenderer` uses on the context meter, so one
number cannot read as two different warnings on two parts of the screen.

  rounds     green -> amber at 60% -> red at 80%. Rounds run out too, and
             running out is how a turn ends with nothing.
  context    the existing thresholds, now with a bar.
  failed     red when non-zero, grey at zero. Zero failures should not shout.
  repeated   amber from three, grey below.
  verdict    replaces the spinner when the turn ends: green done, red failed.

Everything that is only a label is grey, so the coloured things are the ones
worth looking at. The statusline became segments rather than one grey strip -
the left block is amber RUNNING or green READY, because that is the one thing
you glance down for.


A LAYOUT BUG WORTH THE NOTE
---------------------------
The first version sized the label column at 12 and truncated values to fit:

    repeated  contract_status x

...which throws away the count, i.e. the only number on the row. The key column
is now exactly as wide as `contracts`, the longest label, and `KEY_WIDTH`
carries the reason. `contract_status x8` is 18 characters and now fits exactly.


